// lowerthird-demo — a broadcast-style caption for compositing over video: a translucent
// black panel across the foot of the frame, the rest fully transparent, holding a bold
// reference heading over the scripture text. It uses only engine primitives — no document
// package. The pieces are \pagecolor{transparent} (an unpainted page, so everything outside
// the panel shows the video through it), \colorbox[alpha] (the translucent fill), and a
// \parbox (the panel, sized to its text plus \fboxsep padding).
//
// Render as a transparent PNG, one pixel per point, so every length below is in pixels:
//   texish -t png -r 72 scripts/lowerthird-demo.script
// The frame is 1280x720 (720p); for 1080p use 1920x1080 and scale the type up to match.

// Full-bleed panel: it spans the whole image and reaches the bottom edge, so no page margin.
\geometry paperwidth:1280pt paperheight:720pt margin:0
\pagecolor{transparent}

// Push the panel to the foot of the frame.
\vfill

// The panel spans the full 1280px width and is a fixed 240px tall — one third of 720 — so it
// fills the lower third exactly, flush to the bottom. The \parbox is 1260x220px and \fboxsep
// adds 10px of padding on every side (1260+20 = 1280 wide, 220+20 = 240 tall), so the text
// sits just 10px from the panel edge. The content is top-aligned ([t]), so the heading sits
// 10px below the panel's top.
\set fboxsep {10}
\colorbox[0.55]{black}{\parbox[c][220pt][t]{1260pt}{
\color{white}
\set parindent {0}
\font ebgaramond 30 bold
John 3:16--17 (NLT)
\par
\vskip 14
\font ebgaramond 28 regular
For this is how God loved the world: He gave his one and only Son, so that everyone who
believes in him will not perish but have eternal life. God sent his Son into the world not
to judge the world, but to save the world through him.
}}
